IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Adelaide Airport Curfew Act 2000 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE
-- TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00621.txt
-- (compilation No. 7, 14 October 2024). The operator of an aircraft (often a
-- private owner-pilot) asks: "Is this movement in the curfew; is it allowed;
-- is it an offence; if I landed off runway 05, by when must I lodge a
-- return?" Times are legal time in South Australia (s 5).

§ `Nouns`

-- Part 3 Divisions 1-3: the kind of aircraft and its standing.
DECLARE `Aircraft kind` IS ONE OF
    `a propeller aircraft of 34,000 kg or less meeting the Annex noise standards`
    `a jet of 34,000 kg or less of a type the regulations specify`
    `an international aircraft with the Minister's shoulder-period permission`
    `a low noise heavy freight aircraft with the Minister's curfew permission`
    `another aircraft`

-- ss 16-17.
DECLARE `Special circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `search and rescue, a medical emergency or a natural disaster`
    `a declared in-flight emergency`
    `too little fuel to divert`
    `an urgent need for safety, security or to avoid property damage`
    `resuming a flight interrupted by such an emergency`
    `a dispensation from the Minister, kept to its conditions`
    `use in a declared national emergency`
    `none`

DECLARE `Movement` IS ONE OF
    `take-off`
    `landing`

DECLARE `Curfew case` HAS
    `the movement`                                          IS A `Movement`
    `the hour`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `the minute`                                            IS A NUMBER
    `the aircraft`                                          IS A `Aircraft kind`
    -- s 14
    `taxi clearance was received before 11 pm`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the special circumstance`                              IS A `Special circumstance`
    -- s 15(3)
    `it landed on a runway other than 05 for the weather on` IS A MAYBE DATE

DECLARE `Curfew position` HAS
    `it is in the curfew period`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is permitted under Part 3`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `I commit an offence under s 6`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `maximum penalty units`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `the last day to give the return`                       IS A MAYBE DATE

§ `Rules`

GIVEN c IS A `Curfew case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`minutes past midnight for` c MEANS 60 TIMES c's `the hour` PLUS c's `the minute`

-- s 3 curfew period: 11 pm to 6 am.
@ref s 3 curfew period
GIVEN c IS A `Curfew case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is in the curfew` c IF
        `minutes past midnight for` c AT LEAST 1380
    OR  `minutes past midnight for` c LESS THAN 360

-- s 3 curfew shoulder period: 11 pm to midnight and 5 am to 6 am.
@ref s 3 curfew shoulder period
GIVEN c IS A `Curfew case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is in a shoulder period` c IF
        `minutes past midnight for` c AT LEAST 1380
    OR  (    `minutes past midnight for` c AT LEAST 300
         AND `minutes past midnight for` c LESS THAN 360)

-- Part 3: ss 9, 11, 12, 13, 14, 16; s 16(b) covers only a take-off to resume
-- an interrupted flight (changed after the independent pass).
@ref ss 9, 11-14, 16-18
GIVEN c IS A `Curfew case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is permitted` c IF
        (    NOT (c's `the special circumstance` EQUALS `none`)
         AND NOT (    c's `the special circumstance` EQUALS `resuming a flight interrupted by such an emergency`
                  AND c's `the movement` EQUALS `landing`))
    OR  c's `the aircraft` EQUALS `a propeller aircraft of 34,000 kg or less meeting the Annex noise standards`
    OR  c's `the aircraft` EQUALS `a jet of 34,000 kg or less of a type the regulations specify`
    OR  c's `the aircraft` EQUALS `a low noise heavy freight aircraft with the Minister's curfew permission`
    OR  (    c's `the aircraft` EQUALS `an international aircraft with the Minister's shoulder-period permission`
         AND `it is in a shoulder period` c)
    OR  (    c's `the movement` EQUALS `take-off`
         AND c's `taxi clearance was received before 11 pm`)

-- s 6: an operator commits an offence if its conduct results in a take-off or
-- landing in a curfew period, unless Part 3 permits it. 200 penalty units.
@ref s 6
GIVEN c IS A `Curfew case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I commit the offence` c IF
        `it is in the curfew` c
    AND NOT (`it is permitted` c)

-- s 15(3): a return "within 7 days after the landing".
@ref s 15(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Curfew case`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the return deadline for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `it landed on a runway other than 05 for the weather on`
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (d PLUS 7)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@ref ss 3, 6, 9-18
@export default The position of the operator of an aircraft taking off from or landing at Adelaide Airport under the Adelaide Airport Curfew Act 2000 (Cth): whether the movement is in the curfew (11 pm to 6 am, South Australian legal time); whether it is permitted (light propeller aircraft and specified light jets meeting noise standards; international aircraft with permission in the 11 pm and 5 am shoulder hours; permitted low noise heavy freight; take-offs cleared to taxi before 11 pm; emergencies, flights resuming after one, ministerial dispensations and national emergencies: Part 3); whether it is an offence (s 6: 200 penalty units); and the last day to lodge a return after landing on a runway other than 05 for the weather (7 days: s 15(3)). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Curfew case`  @desc The movement and its time, the aircraft and any permission, taxi clearance, any emergency or dispensation, and any weather landing
GIVETH A `Curfew position`
`the curfew position for` c MEANS
    `Curfew position` OF `it is in the curfew` c, `it is permitted` c, `I commit the offence` c,
                         (IF `I commit the offence` c THEN 200 ELSE 0), `the return deadline for` c
